# Client portal UI

Before changing anything a client (`client_admin` or `client_user`) sees, read `docs/client-portal-guide.md` and follow it. Build it in the work order from section 5 of the guide.

Rules that always apply:

- A client sees only: Dashboard, Leads, Kunder in the header, and a dropdown with exactly Virksomhedsoplysninger (`/virksomhed`), Mine indstillinger (`/konto`), and Log ud.
- Auth pages (`/login`, `/logget-ud`, `/auth/*`, `/tilmelding*`) show the Censio logo only: no dropdown, no nav, no language switcher.
- Session data comes from the single session context (`useActiveOrganization` / `useUserProfile` read from it). Do not add new `/api/auth/me` fetches in components. Call `reload()` after any save the header shows.
- Never show demo data to a signed-in client: no `CURRENT_COMPANY`, no localStorage name, picture, or logo, no Hvidbjerg badge default.
- Choose admin vs client UI by role, never by URL. Keep the Censio admin experience unchanged.
- Client route rules live in `lib/layout/client-routes.ts`, used by `middleware.ts`.
- Add user-facing text to both `lib/i18n/locales/da.ts` and `lib/i18n/locales/en.ts`.
